# TEMPLATE — copy to  /pubapps/$PROJECT/islet-explorer/app/shiny_app/.Renviron  on the VM.
# This file lives on the world-readable /pubapps volume, so it MUST NOT contain any secret.
#
# Differences from the on-prem lab .Renviron:
#   - NO R_LIBS_USER   : packages live in the container image's site-library, not a personal lib.
#   - NO on-prem IP    : the public host + SSL come from RC's reverse proxy.
#   - NO KEY line here : the UF Navigator API key is injected at container runtime via the
#                        --env-file in deploy/run.sh. Leaving KEY out of this file is REQUIRED —
#                        readRenviron() would otherwise overwrite the injected value with a blank.
#                        (ai_helpers.R reads Sys.getenv("KEY"), which the injected env satisfies.)

# UF Navigator AI Assistant endpoint (OpenAI-compatible). Reachable from the UF network.
BASE=https://api.ai.it.ufl.edu

# Per-session cap on AI Assistant token spend (mod_ai_assistant_server.R blocks requests once
# the budget is exhausted). MUST be set on a Public Open, no-login endpoint: the default is
# unlimited, and the budget resets per session, so an anonymous visitor could otherwise spend
# the UF-issued key without bound. Anyone can open as many sessions as they like — treat this
# as a per-session brake, not a total. If that is not acceptable, disable the AI Assistant tab.
OPENAI_TOKEN_BUDGET=100000

# reticulate: the anndata venv baked into the container image (deploy/islet-explorer.def).
# Must match the venv path in the image and %environment. If this is wrong, read_h5ad()
# fails and the app SILENTLY falls back to master_results.xlsx (Plot cell-type selector
# goes empty) — so verify it after deploy (smoke test #2 in deploy/README.md).
RETICULATE_PYTHON=/opt/islet-explorer-py/bin/python
